{
 "name": "crash_exit_dual",
 "family": "crash-triggered IN/OUT state machine (default IN) + independent realised-vol leverage tier",
 "hypothesis": "Crash losses at leverage come from the first two or three days of a volatility regime change, which trailing-vol and trend gates see only weeks later. A two-session multi-sigma loss (or an implied-vol jump from an elevated base) is the earliest statistically clean observation of that change, so exiting on it and staying out until shocks stop arriving and vol is falling removes the clustered aftermath, while a default-IN state and a realised-vol tier keep the book levered in the calm regimes where the equity premium at 3x is earned.",
